<article class="article">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/blog">Guides</a> &rsaquo; Google Review Reply Examples for Restaurants</div>
  <div class="tag">Restaurants</div>
  <h1>Google review reply examples for restaurants (2026)</h1>
  <div class="meta">Updated 10 November 2026. Google's reply tips were checked on that date.</div>

  <p>Every review, good or bad, is a chance to show the next diner who you are and how you treat people. The examples below cover the reviews restaurants get most: praise, long waits, cold or wrong food, price, noise, and the situations other businesses rarely face, such as delivery orders, allergies and a booking that went wrong.</p>

  <div class="highlight"><p>A good restaurant reply names the dish or the moment, apologises once for the specific problem, says what changed and gives a direct contact. Write it for the next diner reading the page, not only for the reviewer.</p></div>

  <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
    <a href="#praise">5-star replies</a>
    <a href="#negative">Negative replies</a>
    <a href="#mixed">Mixed reviews</a>
    <a href="#restaurant-only">Only restaurants get these</a>
    <a href="#google">What Google says</a>
    <a href="#faq">Questions</a>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="praise">5-star restaurant review responses</h2>

  <div class="section">
    <h3>Food compliment</h3>
    <div class="stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>
    <div class="review-text">"The pasta carbonara was absolutely incredible. Best I have had outside of Rome."</div>
    <div class="bad-example">
      <div class="bad-label">Wrong: too generic</div>
      <p>Thank you for your kind review! We are glad you enjoyed your meal. Hope to see you again soon.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="example-label">Right: personal and specific</div>
      <p>That means so much, [Name]. Comparing our carbonara to Rome is the highest compliment our chef could receive! We use authentic guanciale imported weekly, and it is wonderful to know the effort shows. Thank you for visiting our Italian restaurant. We look forward to welcoming you back very soon!</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Service compliment</h3>
    <div class="stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>
    <div class="review-text">"Staff were so attentive and friendly. Made our anniversary dinner feel really special."</div>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="example-label">Your reply</div>
      <p>Happy anniversary, [Name]! We are so pleased our team could make your evening memorable. Creating special moments for our guests is exactly why we do what we do at [Restaurant Name]. Your kind words will be shared with the whole team, and they will be thrilled. We hope to celebrate many more occasions with you!</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Overall experience</h3>
    <div class="stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>
    <div class="review-text">"Perfect from start to finish. Atmosphere, food, service: all 10/10."</div>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="example-label">Your reply</div>
      <p>Wow, thank you [Name]! A perfect 10 from you has made our whole team's day. We work incredibly hard on every detail, from the atmosphere to the menu to how our guests feel when they walk out, and it is genuinely wonderful to hear it all came together for you. See you again soon at [Restaurant Name]!</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Praise for a named server</h3>
    <div class="stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</div>
    <div class="review-text">"Our server Luca remembered our order from last time and picked the perfect wine for the lamb."</div>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="example-label">Your reply</div>
      <p>Thank you, [Name]. I'll read this out to Luca before Friday's shift; remembering regulars is what he does best. I'm glad the [wine name] worked with the lamb. See you next time. [Your name], [role]</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="negative">Negative restaurant review responses</h2>

  <div class="section">
    <h3>Food quality complaint</h3>
    <div class="stars" style="color:#EA4335">&#9733;&#9733;&#9734;&#9734;&#9734;</div>
    <div class="review-text">"The steak was overcooked and sent back twice. Very disappointing for the price."</div>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="example-label">Your reply</div>
      <p>We sincerely apologise, [Name]. Having a steak sent back twice is completely unacceptable and falls far below our kitchen standards. We have addressed this directly with our head chef. Please email us at [email] so we can talk it through and put it right.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Waiting time complaint</h3>
    <div class="stars" style="color:#EA4335">&#9733;&#9733;&#9734;&#9734;&#9734;</div>
    <div class="review-text">"Waited 55 minutes for mains on a quiet Tuesday night. Unacceptable."</div>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="example-label">Your reply</div>
      <p>Thank you for your feedback, [Name]. A 55-minute wait on a quiet evening is genuinely not acceptable and we are sorry this was your experience. We have looked into what happened that evening and made changes to our kitchen workflow. Please reach out to us at [email], and we would love the opportunity to show you a much better visit.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Price complaint</h3>
    <div class="stars" style="color:#FBBC05">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9734;&#9734;</div>
    <div class="review-text">"Food was decent but felt overpriced for what you get. Would not rush back."</div>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="example-label">Your reply</div>
      <p>Thank you for your honest feedback, [Name]. We understand that value for money is important and we appreciate you sharing your thoughts. We source all our ingredients locally and freshly daily, which does reflect in our pricing, but we always want guests to feel the experience justified the cost. We would love another chance to impress you. Please visit us again at [Restaurant Name].</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>For long waits, rude staff, surprise charges, fake reviews and other situations that are not specific to restaurants, see the <a href="/blog/negative-review-response-templates">12 negative review templates</a>, each with what to leave out.</p>

  <h2 id="mixed">Mixed review responses (3-4 stars)</h2>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9734;</div>
    <div class="review-text">"Food was great but the noise level was really high. Hard to have a conversation."</div>
    <div class="example">
      <div class="example-label">Your reply</div>
      <p>Thank you, [Name]! We are glad the food hit the mark. You are right that we get lively on busy evenings. We are actually looking at acoustic improvements for later this year. For a quieter experience, our early evening slots before 7pm tend to be more relaxed. We hope to welcome you back to our restaurant under better conditions soon!</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="restaurant-only">Replies for situations only restaurants get</h2>

  <h3>A delivery order that arrived late and cold</h3>
  <div class="review-text">"Ordered for delivery. It took 70 minutes and the food was cold. Won't order again."</div>
  <div class="example">
    <div class="example-label">Your reply</div>
    <p>Hi [Name], thank you for telling us, and I'm sorry. Food that arrives cold after 70 minutes is not what we cook it to be. We've [started checking pickup times with the delivery app / paused delivery when the kitchen is at capacity]. If you'd like to talk it through, my direct line is [phone]. [Your name], [role]</p>
  </div>
  <p class="leave-out"><strong>Leave out:</strong> blaming the courier or the app on its own. Say what you control and what you changed.</p>

  <h3>An allergy that was not handled</h3>
  <div class="review-text">"I told the waiter about my nut allergy and the dish still came with nuts on top. Scary."</div>
  <div class="example">
    <div class="example-label">Your reply</div>
    <p>Hi [Name], thank you for telling us. I'm very sorry. An allergy request has to be right every time, and this one wasn't. I'm going through what happened with the team today. Please call me on [phone] so I can hear it from you directly. [Your name], [role]</p>
  </div>
  <p class="leave-out"><strong>Leave out:</strong> anything about the guest's health or what they ate beyond what they wrote, and any promise that your kitchen is allergen-free. If someone needed medical care, get advice before you reply in public.</p>

  <h3>A booking that went wrong</h3>
  <div class="review-text">"We booked weeks ahead for my mum's 70th. Our table had been given away and we waited 30 minutes."</div>
  <div class="example">
    <div class="example-label">Your reply</div>
    <p>Hi [Name], I'm so sorry. Giving away a table booked for your mum's 70th is a mistake we should not have made. Since then we've [changed how reserved tables are marked on the floor plan on busy nights]. Please call me on [phone]; I'd like to hear how the evening went. [Your name], [role]</p>
  </div>
  <p class="leave-out"><strong>Leave out:</strong> a free dessert or voucher in the public reply. Google asks owners to avoid deals and promotions in replies, so keep any goodwill gesture private.</p>

  <h3>A demand for a free meal, or a bad review follows</h3>
  <p>If a guest threatens a one-star review unless you comp the meal, or a burst of one-star reviews is followed by a demand for money or food, do not pay or negotiate. Google calls extortion scams a serious policy violation and says: &ldquo;Do not engage with or pay the malicious individuals.&rdquo; Save screenshots of every demand and report it through <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/16404809" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's extortion report form</a>. A public reply is optional and should stay neutral.</p>

  <h2 id="google">What Google's reply tips say</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data stack">
    <thead><tr><th>Google's tip</th><th>In a restaurant reply</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td data-label="Google's tip">&ldquo;Address the reviewer by name and acknowledge their specific feedback.&rdquo;</td><td data-label="In a restaurant reply">Name the dish, the occasion or the server the guest mentioned.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Google's tip">&ldquo;Apologize when appropriate.&rdquo;</td><td data-label="In a restaurant reply">One apology, for the specific problem.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Google's tip">&ldquo;Keep it short and simple.&rdquo;</td><td data-label="In a restaurant reply">Three to five sentences.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Google's tip">&ldquo;Respond in a timely manner.&rdquo;</td><td data-label="In a restaurant reply">In <a href="https://www.brightlocal.com/research/local-consumer-review-survey/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BrightLocal's 2026 survey</a>, 81% of consumers expected a reply within a week.</td></tr>
      <tr><td data-label="Google's tip">&ldquo;Instead of sending the same &lsquo;thank you&rsquo; to everyone, focus on reviews where you can share a helpful update&rdquo;</td><td data-label="In a restaurant reply">Vary the wording and answer what the guest actually wrote.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Google also says replies should not &ldquo;offer deals or promotions&rdquo;. Source: <a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/3474122" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Business Profile Help, tips to write better review replies</a>. The full process, from verifying your profile to what happens after you press Reply, is in <a href="/blog/how-to-respond-to-google-reviews">How to respond to Google reviews</a>.</p>

  <h2>Writing tips for restaurant replies</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Name the dish, the occasion or the staff member the guest mentioned</li>
    <li>Say "our restaurant" or your cuisine only where it reads naturally; Google has not said that keywords in replies affect ranking</li>
    <li>Vary your wording: Google&#39;s own reply tips advise against sending the same thank-you to everyone</li>
    <li>Reply within a few days: in <a href="https://www.brightlocal.com/research/local-consumer-review-survey/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BrightLocal&#39;s 2026 survey</a>, 81% of consumers expected a reply within a week</li>
  </ul>

